' Pattern component notes
note bottom of BasicSingleton
  <b>Basic Singleton (NOT Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Private constructor prevents instantiation
  • Static instance variable
  • Static getInstance() creates instance lazily
  • Simple but NOT thread-safe

  <b>Problem:</b>
  Multiple threads can create multiple instances
  if getInstance() is called simultaneously.
end note

note bottom of ThreadSafeSingletonSynchronizedMethod
  <b>Synchronized Method (Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Entire getInstance() method is synchronized
  • Guarantees thread safety
  • Simple to implement

  <b>Trade-off:</b>
  Performance overhead - synchronization
  on EVERY call, even after initialization.
end note

note bottom of ThreadSafeSingletonDoubleCheckedLocking
  <b>Double-Checked Locking (Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Uses volatile keyword for instance
  • Checks instance twice (before and after lock)
  • Synchronizes only during initialization

  <b>Advantage:</b>
  Minimal synchronization overhead -
  only locks when instance is null.
end note

note bottom of ThreadSafeSingletonEagerInitialization
  <b>Eager Initialization (Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Instance created at class loading time
  • No synchronization needed
  • JVM guarantees thread safety

  <b>Trade-off:</b>
  Instance created even if never used.
  Not suitable for resource-heavy objects.
end note

note bottom of ThreadSafeSingletonInitializationOnDemand
  <b>Initialization-on-Demand Holder (Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Uses static inner class (Holder)
  • JVM handles synchronization
  • Lazy initialization without explicit locking

  <b>Advantage:</b>
  Best of both worlds - lazy initialization
  AND thread safety without synchronization.
  Recommended approach for most cases.
end note

note bottom of EnumSingleton
  <b>Enum Singleton (Thread-Safe)</b>
  • Uses Java enum type
  • JVM guarantees single instance
  • Serialization-safe by default
  • Cannot be instantiated via reflection

  <b>Advantage:</b>
  Simplest and safest implementation.
  Joshua Bloch recommendation in
  "Effective Java".
end note

note bottom of CommissionCalculation
  <b>Domain Model</b>
  The object managed by singleton.
  Contains commission calculation logic.
end note

' Legend
note bottom of EnumSingleton
  <b>Singleton Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Private Constructor:</b> Prevents
  external instantiation of the class.

  <b>Static Instance Variable:</b> Holds
  the single instance of the class.

  <b>Static getInstance() Method:</b>
  Provides global access point to
  the singleton instance.

  <b>Key Considerations:</b>
  • Thread safety requirements
  • Lazy vs. Eager initialization
  • Performance impact
  • Serialization handling
  • Reflection attacks
end note

